    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T22:55:51Z",
    "body": "Triage (contributor agent, checked on main c442118). Here is what exists today and a split.\n\n**Today**\n- **Tools are numbers only.** A tool is a parametric record; its holder is one cylinder (`holder_d` / `holder_len`).\n- **Mill checks judge stacked cylinders** (shank, holder, fixture sweeps).\n- **The lathe sim doesn't judge the holder at all.** Only the insert is checked, so the asymmetric Capto/KM case isn't covered.\n- **A STEP importer already exists.** Fixtures already use it (a fixture is a STEP model with a tag), so reading vendor files is solved. The work is placing, judging and showing them.\n\n**Split**\n- #368: tool bodies from STEP, milling. Import and numeric placement; checks use the body's revolved envelope (conservative). **Claimed next.**\n- #369: lathe holder bodies judged against the revolved stock (radial clearance along Z). This is the part this issue most wants; it builds on #368.\n- #370: automatic alignment from the vendor package's tool coordinate systems (ISO 13399 / GTC), once the names are confirmed from public docs.\n- #371: GUI: pick tip and axis in the tool editor, draw the real body in the viewport and sim (shares data with #93).\n\nSaving bodies in the tool library file follows once #348 (the library file format) merges.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
