    "body": "fix on issue/361-vendor-tool-models · PR #1043 · pinned by vendor_tool_body (3: a STEP lathe holder placed off its model frame is judged and its mirror stands clear; a coarsely meshed STEP is refused as a body; the placement preview is the command's reading), mcp_tool_body (5) and egui_app::tests::tool_body_lathe (6) · merges at the next cut\n\nPartial (`Refs`): the triage split (#368, #369, #370, #371) had all shipped; this PR makes the lathe holder body reachable from the tool editor and MCP, and refuses a reduced-fidelity STEP as a tool body. Still owed, filed as sub-issues (each Part of #361):\n- #1037 (P1) the lathe holder body judged against workholding and fixtures, not only part and stock\n- #1038 the lathe body drawn in the simulation and viewport\n- #1039 a lathe placement from a file's ISO 13399 coordinate systems\n- #1040 a tool assembled from several vendor bodies (the ISO 26622 / 26623 interfaces)\n- #1041 a reduced-fidelity body judged grown by its chord error instead of refused\n- imported bodies in `.camtools` files ride #889 (commented there)",
